Haven't read this newsgroup in ages, and I'm running a very old
version of Nethack (2.2) on my PC. Got a couple questions about
unicorns.

First, I left some gems in a room, and when I came back, the gems were
gone but there was a unicorn there. Do unicorns steal gems? (I know
they like them, but I'd never had them stolen before.)

Second, I accidentally killed one unicorn. I was very cautious about
praying afterward, because I think the gods are fond of unicorns. I
eventually figured I'd gotten back into their good graces in the usual
way, and prayed, and everything was okay. Did I need to make the
atonement, or can unicorns be killed freely? I've got one level with 7
of the buggers running around on it, including the one who lifted my
gems, and I'd really like to be rid of them.

Third, if I kill a unicorn that's holding gems, will I get them back,
the way you can get money back from a leprechaun?

And a bonus question, which has nothing to do with unicorns. I'm
wearing my trusty ring of polymorph control. I have walked into a
couple of polymorph traps, and changed into my favorite creature. But
a couple of times it hasn't worked, and I've become a "new man" or
"new woman." Do the rings have a certain chance of failure, or what?
It is most annoying to have a character with over 100,000 experience
points suddenly revert to a 12th level character.

Thanks for answers.
